# Token Budget — Eager Context

Claude Code loads these files on EVERY conversation turn. Keep them lean.

## Budget limits

Loose, realistic ceilings — measured on live projects, not aspirational. The goal
is a limit you can actually meet, so the numbers get checked. Run the measurer
(below) and fill `Current`.

| Component | Budget | Current |
|---|---|---|
| CLAUDE.md | ~2,200 tok | — |
| Rules (always-loaded, no `paths`) | ~2,000 tok total | — |
| Agents | ~2,700 tok total | — |
| Skills metadata (descriptions) | ~1,300 tok total | — |
| Memory index (`MEMORY.md`) | ~1,500 tok | — |
| **Total eager** | **~10,000 tok** | **—** |

These are the five categories that actually load every turn. Agents and the memory
index are the two most often forgotten — count them.

## Per-component guidance

- Path-scoped rule: keep lean, but it only loads on its paths — not eager everywhere.
- A rule with NO `paths` loads every turn — that is the expensive kind; keep those few.
- Agent: no hard cap. The biggest (`doc-updater`) is ~1,600 tok and earns it — don't
  shrink it by moving its procedure out (the agent then invents what it can't read).
- Skill description: ~100 tokens (~50 words) each.
- CLAUDE.md over ~2,200 tok → move project-specific detail to path-scoped rules.

## Maintenance rules

- Before adding to CLAUDE.md: can it go in a path-scoped rule instead?
- Before adding a rule: does it really apply to ALL contexts in that path?
- Before adding a skill: will it be used at least 1x/month?
- Verify budget: `python .claude/count-context-tokens.py` (if available)
